<%# What neither the pasted list nor the table above can show: the SAP action
    writes to more documents than it examined, and the ticket action never
    replaces anything even when the row says a document already exists. %>
<% if batch.action.id == "wap" %>
  <%= ui_callout_box :warning, icon: "circle-exclamation", icon_type: :solid do %>
    <strong>Every SAP and Staff Credential each person holds gets this date.</strong>
    The table above names the one document that was checked, but the date lands on all of that
    person's qualified, claimed and banked passes and credentials. Ones already submitted are
    left alone.
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <%= ui_callout_box :info, icon: "circle-info", icon_type: :solid do %>
    <strong>Each line creates a new document, marked qualified.</strong>
    Nothing is overwritten. A line for someone who already holds that type gives them a second
    one — those rows are the amber ones above.
    <code>LSD</code> and <code>VPLSD</code> are the exception: those are recorded as claimed,
    because an LSD item is only entered once the recipient has asked for it.
  <% end %>
<% end %>
